1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,361
Did you cut this yourself today?

2
00:00:02,386 --> 00:00:03,195
Yes, that's right

3
00:00:03,220 --> 00:00:04,980
Where did all this meat go?

4
00:00:06,166 --> 00:00:07,026
At this rate,

5
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:08,920
I don’t think I can pay you today

6
00:00:09,033 --> 00:00:10,715
There were bones, bones everywhere

7
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,395
Aren’t you the sunbae here?

8
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:11,960
That’s right

9
00:00:12,306 --> 00:00:13,813
If you teach like this,
who’s going to take responsibility?

10
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:14,766
Oh no…

11
00:00:15,366 --> 00:00:17,759
Isn’t it the senior's job
to manage the juniors properly?

12
00:00:19,654 --> 00:00:20,320
(Asa/ Rora/ BABYMONSTER)
Asa

13
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:22,156
Do you think you can film Workdol
while on a world tour?

14
00:00:22,156 --> 00:00:23,457
Washing dishes?

15
00:00:23,457 --> 00:00:24,458
Cleaning the grill?

16
00:00:24,458 --> 00:00:26,226
I'll do whatever needs to be done

17
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:27,761
(Cheating)

18
00:00:27,764 --> 00:00:29,096
Don't look too closely

19
00:00:29,097 --> 00:00:29,930
(Just wait)

20
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:31,665
Do you not understand
even if I write the lines?

21
00:00:31,665 --> 00:00:32,867
(Memory issue)

22
00:00:32,868 --> 00:00:33,667
It's okay

23
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:34,402
(Take two)
Asa

24
00:00:34,402 --> 00:00:36,203
Do you think you can film Workdol
while on a world tour?

25
00:00:36,203 --> 00:00:37,104
Washing dishes?

26
00:00:37,104 --> 00:00:38,172
Cleaning the grill?

27
00:00:38,172 --> 00:00:39,807
I'll do whatever needs to be done

28
00:00:39,807 --> 00:00:41,542
Don't let anyone else decide my worth

29
00:00:41,542 --> 00:00:43,077
My life is just getting started,

30
00:00:43,077 --> 00:00:43,844
and I'm going to

31
00:00:43,844 --> 00:00:46,147
live eating only the finest steak

32
00:00:46,147 --> 00:00:47,748
So, where am I working today?

33
00:00:47,748 --> 00:00:48,949
At a steakhouse

34
00:00:48,949 --> 00:00:50,284
Think I can sneak a bite?

35
00:00:50,285 --> 00:00:51,786
I can probably take a bite, right?

36
00:00:52,586 --> 00:00:53,454
(Rich man's hotspot Wolfgang)

37
00:00:54,254 --> 00:00:55,522
(Steakhouse part-timer)

38
00:00:55,522 --> 00:00:56,723
I've heard

39
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,458
this place is really expensive

40
00:00:58,458 --> 00:01:02,162
(A place where the wealthy come to dine)
They say a lot of rich folks
visit this steakhouse

41
00:01:02,162 --> 00:01:04,531
So today, Asa unnie is treating me to steak

42
00:01:04,531 --> 00:01:05,632
Um, let me

43
00:01:05,633 --> 00:01:05,966
think

44
00:01:05,972 --> 00:01:07,033
about that for a second

45
00:01:07,033 --> 00:01:08,101
My bank account is

46
00:01:08,101 --> 00:01:09,936
pretty much empty right now

47
00:01:09,936 --> 00:01:11,705
(Actually came here to make money)

48
00:01:11,705 --> 00:01:13,974
(3-00 PM - Heading to work)
Since I'm a bit more experienced

49
00:01:13,974 --> 00:01:16,109
(Workdol experienced worker's bluff)
- Follow me
- Because you're experienced

50
00:01:16,109 --> 00:01:19,145
But today, since many
high-profile people are coming,

51
00:01:19,145 --> 00:01:20,480
let's maintain our dignity

52
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:20,947
Right

53
00:01:20,947 --> 00:01:23,283
How's everyone doing?

54
00:01:23,283 --> 00:01:24,684
How's everyone doing?

55
00:01:24,684 --> 00:01:26,786
(Dignity that raises doubts about her hometown)
- In this kind of vibe
- It's strange

56
00:01:26,786 --> 00:01:27,954
Hello

57
00:01:27,954 --> 00:01:28,655
Hello

58
00:01:28,655 --> 00:01:32,158
Welcome to our Wolfgang Steakhouse!

59
00:01:32,158 --> 00:01:34,227
(Han Soomin)
(3rd year)
We're the best steakhouse in South Korea

60
00:01:34,227 --> 00:01:36,696
I've heard that many VIPs

61
00:01:36,696 --> 00:01:39,666
and business people come here often

62
00:01:39,666 --> 00:01:42,302
They host parties and events as well

63
00:01:42,302 --> 00:01:45,205
(Q. Who was the prettiest?)
Then, is there an artist
who left the biggest impression on you?

64
00:01:45,205 --> 00:01:46,339
For me, it's BLACKPINK

65
00:01:46,339 --> 00:01:46,873
Uh

66
00:01:46,873 --> 00:01:47,974
Oh, wowww

67
00:01:47,974 --> 00:01:48,642
Amazing

68
00:01:48,642 --> 00:01:51,211
(Feeling that YG hype)

69
00:01:51,213 --> 00:01:52,712
(Stop)
Before we get started,

70
00:01:52,712 --> 00:01:54,748
let me just say a few things

71
00:01:54,748 --> 00:01:55,782
The kitchen can be

72
00:01:55,782 --> 00:01:56,750
a really dangerous place

73
00:01:56,750 --> 00:01:57,717
Knives can go flying around

74
00:01:57,718 --> 00:01:58,184
Whoa!

75
00:01:58,184 --> 00:01:59,586
And flames can suddenly flare up
all over the place

76
00:01:59,586 --> 00:02:00,353
Whoa!

77
00:02:00,353 --> 00:02:00,754
So

78
00:02:00,754 --> 00:02:01,988
you need to get yourself in line

79
00:02:01,988 --> 00:02:02,789
(Yes, sir)
and

80
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:03,823
start working with discipline

81
00:02:03,823 --> 00:02:05,792
(Nervously alert)
- Yes, understood
- Got it?

82
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:09,062
(3:30 PM - Meat prep)
You'll now follow me and work on the meat

83
00:02:09,062 --> 00:02:10,830
If you two don't do it right,

84
00:02:10,830 --> 00:02:11,765
you're going to get scolded

85
00:02:11,766 --> 00:02:13,466
(Is this the start of strict discipline...?)
We'll get in trouble...?

86
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:15,402
How should I address you?

87
00:02:15,402 --> 00:02:17,771
(Strictly)
Please call me Chef

88
00:02:17,771 --> 00:02:18,738
Soomin

89
00:02:18,741 --> 00:02:19,340
senpai

90
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:20,040
Soomin

91
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:20,641
senpai

92
00:02:20,641 --> 00:02:22,309
Chef Soomin to you

93
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:23,377
That's really, really cute

94
00:02:23,377 --> 00:02:25,012
(Disarmed)
In Japan, they'd call him senpai

95
00:02:25,012 --> 00:02:27,414
Now, let's head into the aging room

96
00:02:27,415 --> 00:02:28,315
(Serious)
It's kind of like a trade secret

97
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:29,350
Oh wow

98
00:02:29,352 --> 00:02:30,384
A trade secret

99
00:02:30,384 --> 00:02:33,554
(A rather feeble warning)
- You can't tell anyone about this
- Seriously, don't tell anyone

100
00:02:33,554 --> 00:02:35,155
(Entering)
These are some
seriously expensive cuts of meat

101
00:02:35,156 --> 00:02:36,223
Amazing

102
00:02:36,223 --> 00:02:37,691
That's a huge amount

103
00:02:37,691 --> 00:02:40,327
We carefully select just 2% of American beef,

104
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:44,631
(Only the finest, handpicked beef)
and then dry-age it ourselves
using our own expertise

105
00:02:44,631 --> 00:02:48,335
(Q. How much is all this?)
So, about how much are these meats worth?

106
00:02:48,335 --> 00:02:49,469
If you pack it all in,

107
00:02:49,469 --> 00:02:50,337
nearly a billion won?

108
00:02:50,337 --> 00:02:51,538
Whoa!

109
00:02:51,538 --> 00:02:52,372
A billion won

110
00:02:52,372 --> 00:02:53,941
(Time to snatch and run)
Let's grab one

111
00:02:53,941 --> 00:02:55,375
How many kilos is each one?

112
00:02:55,375 --> 00:02:56,577
Each one weighs 15 kilos

113
00:02:56,577 --> 00:02:57,277
Whoa

114
00:02:57,277 --> 00:02:57,845
On average,

115
00:02:57,845 --> 00:02:59,847
- they're about 13 to 15 kilos each
- Wow, that's really heavy

116
00:02:59,847 --> 00:03:02,883
(Conspiring openly)
We could just carry it together
when we head out

117
00:03:02,883 --> 00:03:06,119
(Time to move the meat)
Now we have to take this meat outside

118
00:03:06,119 --> 00:03:08,288
(Trying to act tough)
Whoa, Asa, there's no way you can lift this

119
00:03:08,288 --> 00:03:09,890
(Offended)
I've been working out lately

120
00:03:10,487 --> 00:03:12,492
Asa works out

121
00:03:12,492 --> 00:03:14,194
(This is tough)
Oh, wait a second

122
00:03:14,194 --> 00:03:17,497
(The dream of embezzlement is gone)
Let’s just share one between us,
this isn’t going to work

123
00:03:17,497 --> 00:03:19,066
Let’s start with

124
00:03:19,066 --> 00:03:21,234
(Performance)
the trimming step first

125
00:03:21,234 --> 00:03:22,603
Don’t act like an idol

126
00:03:22,603 --> 00:03:23,704
Keep it classy

127
00:03:23,704 --> 00:03:25,872
(Flirting confiscation for a moment)
Okay

128
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:28,575
Alright, let’s try trimming this

129
00:03:28,575 --> 00:03:30,877
(The process of removing unnecessary parts
to improve meat quality)
You cut away all the inedible bits

130
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:32,679
Alright, let me show you first,

131
00:03:32,679 --> 00:03:34,414
and then you can try it yourself

132
00:03:34,414 --> 00:03:34,781
Okay

133
00:03:34,781 --> 00:03:35,949
(Sneak peek)
You have to watch closely, Asa

134
00:03:35,949 --> 00:03:36,917
I'm watching carefully

135
00:03:36,917 --> 00:03:38,552
Don't mess up the meat, okay?

136
00:03:38,552 --> 00:03:39,019
We'll get complaints if you do

137
00:03:39,019 --> 00:03:40,487
They say this is tenderloin

138
00:03:40,487 --> 00:03:41,888
Doesn't that make you feel tender?

139
00:03:41,888 --> 00:03:43,423
(Seriously...)

140
00:03:43,423 --> 00:03:45,826
Okay, always be careful with knives

141
00:03:45,826 --> 00:03:48,295
(Right up to it)
Watch your fingers

142
00:03:48,295 --> 00:03:50,664
(Trimming the meat
1. Removing the fat layer)
Carefully trim away the fat

143
00:03:50,664 --> 00:03:53,667
(2. Remove any unnecessary parts)
Trim off all the excess meat like this

144
00:03:53,667 --> 00:03:57,371
(3. Trimming)
- Make it look nice
- Now it's just pure tenderloin left

145
00:03:57,371 --> 00:03:58,705
If you slip with the knife,

146
00:03:58,705 --> 00:04:00,007
you'll lose ten
or twenty thousand won just like that

147
00:04:00,008 --> 00:04:00,707
Whoa!

148
00:04:00,707 --> 00:04:02,509
Have you ever gotten in trouble
for slicing something wrong?

149
00:04:02,509 --> 00:04:03,443
Oh, plenty of times

150
00:04:03,443 --> 00:04:04,211
Get over to the freezer

151
00:04:04,211 --> 00:04:04,845
It was kind of like that vibe

152
00:04:06,847 --> 00:04:09,183
(Turns out, it was the room of truth..?)
Luckily, I wasn't actually hit

153
00:04:09,183 --> 00:04:11,118
(Straight into action)
Let's have you two give it a try

154
00:04:11,118 --> 00:04:12,152
I used to be

155
00:04:12,152 --> 00:04:13,220
a bit of a kid chef, you know

156
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:14,388
Oh

157
00:04:14,388 --> 00:04:17,124
(Experienced chef)
- That's right, you were a kids' chef
- I can trust you in the kitchen

158
00:04:17,125 --> 00:04:17,591
What about Asa?

159
00:04:17,591 --> 00:04:18,859
I'm pretty good at cooking

160
00:04:18,859 --> 00:04:21,028
I even make galbijjim

161
00:04:21,029 --> 00:04:22,629
(For real?)

162
00:04:23,630 --> 00:04:25,832
(Professional-level air slicing)

163
00:04:25,832 --> 00:04:27,200
You're not able to use a knife at all?

164
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:29,169
(How did you even make galbijjim?)
Hold on a second

165
00:04:29,169 --> 00:04:31,338
(Extra lesson)
Let me show you one more time

166
00:04:31,338 --> 00:04:32,839
(Meanwhile, straight back to chopping)
Just follow the bone down

167
00:04:32,839 --> 00:04:35,375
(Is this what experience looks like?)

168
00:04:35,376 --> 00:04:36,443
Aren't I doing pretty well?

169
00:04:36,443 --> 00:04:37,577
Yeah, you're doing great

170
00:04:37,577 --> 00:04:40,313
(Slicing through with ease)
- I think you should get hired here
- You're a real catch, you know?

171
00:04:40,313 --> 00:04:42,983
(Finished 5 pieces in no time)
I think it's best to stop here for now

172
00:04:42,983 --> 00:04:44,084
Hold on a second

173
00:04:44,084 --> 00:04:45,719
Whoa, is this right?

174
00:04:45,719 --> 00:04:47,020
(Couldn't even finish one piece here)

175
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:48,355
(In the middle of a battle)
What are you doing?

176
00:04:48,355 --> 00:04:49,789
Asa, what are you thinking about right now?

177
00:04:50,857 --> 00:04:51,725
Huh?

178
00:04:51,725 --> 00:04:53,526
I don't think
we should talk to Asa right now

179
00:04:53,526 --> 00:04:55,328
(Slide)
I'm super focused right now

180
00:04:55,329 --> 00:04:56,162
No way

181
00:04:56,162 --> 00:04:56,796
No way?

182
00:04:56,796 --> 00:04:57,364
We're doomed

183
00:04:57,364 --> 00:04:59,032
(So doomed)
It's doomed

184
00:04:59,032 --> 00:05:00,900
I told you, don't talk to me

185
00:05:00,902 --> 00:05:01,701
Mmm-hmm

186
00:05:01,701 --> 00:05:03,069
We need to set the bone

187
00:05:03,069 --> 00:05:03,703
Ah

188
00:05:03,703 --> 00:05:04,438
(Refocusing)

189
00:05:04,441 --> 00:05:05,139
Uh

190
00:05:05,141 --> 00:05:06,340
She messed it up

191
00:05:06,341 --> 00:05:08,675
(Still cutting into the money)
Chef, we've got 20,000 won deducted here

192
00:05:08,675 --> 00:05:10,344
It's time to summon the fridge

193
00:05:10,344 --> 00:05:12,312
(To the room of truth)
Follow me to the freezer

194
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,413
Oh no

195
00:05:13,413 --> 00:05:14,581
unnie, if you're dragged away later,
I'm not responsible

196
00:05:14,581 --> 00:05:15,782
Looks like I'm getting dragged away

197
00:05:15,782 --> 00:05:17,584
It's not bad? Shall we try a bit more here?

198
00:05:18,418 --> 00:05:19,452
What else should we do?

199
00:05:19,452 --> 00:05:21,454
She needs to learn again

200
00:05:21,454 --> 00:05:23,623
Can you eat this?

201
00:05:23,623 --> 00:05:24,858
- No
- No, you can't

202
00:05:24,858 --> 00:05:27,160
- You can't eat it
- So what do we do? Eliminate

203
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,061
Asa

204
00:05:28,061 --> 00:05:29,229
We can't let Asa get eliminated

205
00:05:29,229 --> 00:05:30,163
(Be careful)

206
00:05:30,164 --> 00:05:31,932
What if Asa gets eliminated?

207
00:05:31,932 --> 00:05:33,800
Now, you'll also get to meet

208
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:36,469
your sunbaes in the second floor kitchen

209
00:05:36,469 --> 00:05:37,003
We're in trouble

210
00:05:37,003 --> 00:05:38,305
I think we're really
going to get scolded then

211
00:05:38,305 --> 00:05:40,140
(Prepare to get wrecked)

212
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:42,840
(4:30 PM - Grilling Training)
- Hello
- I'm a new recruit

213
00:05:42,864 --> 00:05:44,524
Before we start grilling this,

214
00:05:44,660 --> 00:05:46,053
let's get our head chef

215
00:05:46,053 --> 00:05:47,655
Our big boss

216
00:05:47,656 --> 00:05:48,256
(Yikes)
Whoa

217
00:05:48,256 --> 00:05:49,090
Let's have

218
00:05:49,090 --> 00:05:50,658
the chief inspect this first

219
00:05:50,658 --> 00:05:51,526
Get ready to be scolded

220
00:05:51,526 --> 00:05:53,361
What are you saying?
You should get ready

221
00:05:53,361 --> 00:05:56,564
(Head chef appears)
Hello

222
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:58,065
(A step back)
How do you do

223
00:05:58,065 --> 00:05:58,633
Whoa

224
00:05:58,633 --> 00:06:01,435
Did you cut this yourself today?

225
00:06:01,435 --> 00:06:02,303
Yes, that's right

226
00:06:02,303 --> 00:06:03,905
Would you mind if I check it over?

227
00:06:03,906 --> 00:06:05,606
Please do

228
00:06:05,606 --> 00:06:08,276
(Trimming evaluation begins)
With eagle eyes

229
00:06:08,276 --> 00:06:10,111
(Nervous...)

230
00:06:10,112 --> 00:06:11,145
(Tilts head)

231
00:06:11,145 --> 00:06:13,247
Where did all this meat go?

232
00:06:13,247 --> 00:06:15,383
(The culprit)

233
00:06:15,383 --> 00:06:16,250
At this rate,

234
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:17,718
I don’t think I can pay you today

235
00:06:17,719 --> 00:06:18,085
Uh...

236
00:06:18,085 --> 00:06:19,787
No way

237
00:06:19,787 --> 00:06:21,656
(It’s the bones)
There were bones, bones everywhere

238
00:06:21,656 --> 00:06:22,490
Aren’t you the sunbae here?

239
00:06:22,492 --> 00:06:23,190
That’s right

240
00:06:23,193 --> 00:06:24,893
If you teach like this,
who’s going to take responsibility?

241
00:06:24,893 --> 00:06:26,461
(Nervous/ Super nervous)
Oh, no

242
00:06:26,461 --> 00:06:28,630
(Getting a harsh scolding)
Isn’t it the senior's job
to manage the juniors properly?

243
00:06:28,630 --> 00:06:29,497
Yes, sir

244
00:06:29,497 --> 00:06:30,899
How are we going to
take responsibility for this?

245
00:06:30,899 --> 00:06:32,300
(Awkward silence)

246
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:33,468
Boss

247
00:06:33,469 --> 00:06:34,369
We'll do the dishes

248
00:06:34,369 --> 00:06:35,603
Next time,

249
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:37,038
we'll invite you to our concert

250
00:06:37,038 --> 00:06:39,207
(Grin)
Oh, really?

251
00:06:39,207 --> 00:06:40,475
(In a flash)
Alright, I'll take responsibility for this

252
00:06:40,475 --> 00:06:41,376
(Speechless)

253
00:06:41,376 --> 00:06:42,177
Thank you

254
00:06:42,177 --> 00:06:44,245
(Thanks for the smooth deal)

255
00:06:44,245 --> 00:06:47,048
Now, let's get started grilling the meat

256
00:06:47,048 --> 00:06:48,349
What should we do first?

257
00:06:48,349 --> 00:06:49,250
Season it

258
00:06:49,251 --> 00:06:49,784
Right

259
00:06:49,784 --> 00:06:52,153
(Steak cooking)
(1. Salt it well)
You need to sprinkle salt evenly from the shaker

260
00:06:52,153 --> 00:06:54,289
Let it go, let it go

261
00:06:54,289 --> 00:06:57,325
- That's right, evenly
- Evenly, evenly, evenly, evenly

262
00:06:57,325 --> 00:07:00,662
(2. Put it in the broiler)
We'll lift it using tongs

263
00:07:00,662 --> 00:07:01,496
